# Line endings are normalised to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# `text=auto` alone would only fix what is stored, which was never the problem:
# every blob in this repository was already LF. `eol=lf` is the half that
# matters, because it fixes what is *checked out* - and the defect this file
# exists to prevent lived in the working tree.
#
# A C# raw string literal carries the newlines of the source file it is written
# in. With core.autocrlf on and no rule here, the generation prompt was CRLF on
# a Windows laptop and LF in CI, so the same prompt hashed two different ways
# and two runs of identical wording were recorded as different experiments.
# See the 2026-11-07 amendment to ADR-034.
#
# GenerationPrompt.Sha256 now normalises before hashing, so the hash is correct
# whatever a checkout does. This file removes the condition rather than relying
# on every future value that crosses into a key remembering to defend itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep CRLF where a tool requires it on Windows.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
